# Entry Main. A supplied actual reaches the input of a structural call when `return` stands before that input in the
# data: the field return describes a result and takes no number among the inputs, and the result it describes is the
# value of the call (step 21.7 K2). The data of `add` is its parent `Add`; its inputs are `x` alone; the result is int.
# `Add\add(x := 7)` gives 8, `Add\add(9)` gives 10: the named and the positional supply fill that input alike.
# Norm: the book #structural-call; #return-in-data; #fn-signature.
int: named 0
int: positional 0
Add:
    return: int
    int: x 0
    add:
        return: x + 1
    end: add
end: Add
Main:
    node\named := Add\add(x := 7)
    node\positional := Add\add(9)
